Again, I finally end my suffer from this 2.5 D power point model resident evil game. However, unlike resident evil 0 or other games in the Franchise, I pretty much enjoy this one. This is a typical resident evil series that you: 

1. Find you somewhere inside a mansion, a ship, a house or a village;
2. You encounter monsters that being infected by T-virus, G-virus, etc..;
3. You are tracking your partners and solving puzzles  
4. Eventually you end up in a lab and know this is T-virus, G or whatever;
5. You fight the final Boss, sometimes it is wisker, or it is Eveline or it is Amadan...;

I have to be honest that I cannot really enjoy this 2.5 D PPT tank shooting zombie mode although I am 
very good at TPS in following series especially in original RE4, 7, 8 etc.. Therefore, the way to skip this kind
of annoying Tank shooting zombie mode in this one is to start a trainer:

1. Open infinite save; 
2. Get a gun with infinite ammo; 
3. Open a step-by-step walk through, so you do not waste your precious time wondering in this
mansion and then find out "Oh, I forgot pick up that key item that is not that obviously" !

Overall, with the trainer to skip those out-dated part, it is a fun game. I would say it is a downgraded 
RE7 where downgraded is in terms of "game fighting mechanism".

However, if you are a really fan plus endless pointless free time, you can try beat the game in its original, but I highly assume you will be mad at some point, because remember, you can only hear not see animal in certain darn scenarios.

Resident Evil 1 is a great game even 25 years after the release.  This remastered version still gives a pleasant experience today and runs great on steam deck as well.  The only flaw probably is the direction control especially when switching camera.  My character has been running in circles several times due to this issue and it could be frustrating at times.

Achievements in this games requires several runs.  There are several challenging achievements such as speed run 3 hours,  real survivor mode and CQC FTW.  

I played in the sequence below:
1st and 2nd run:  Chris and Jill each run on low difficulty and get best endings;
3rd run:  Jill No save run on very easy;
4th run:  Jill 3 hours speed run on normal;
5th run:  Jill real survival run, it will get you hard difficulty achievement at the same time;
6th run:  Chris CQC FTW and invisible enemy at the same time on very easy.
If you are familiar with the game, some of the runs can be combined, but a minimum of 4 runs are required for all achievements.

This is the HD Remaster of the 2002 Remake of the original Resident Evil.

[u]Pros[/u]
+ The new models look very nice;
+ Very faithful to the 1996 original game.
+ Real Survivor Mode gives you a really good challenge, with the game set to Hard difficulty, no auto-aim, no Infinite Weapons and the item boxes are no longer interconnected.

[u]Cons[/u]
- The background textures and FMVs are extremely low resolution, Capcom should have done a better job with such a Remaster;
- You cannot discard any items on your inventory, except for keys when prompted;
- Cloud saving is a bit slow;
- Loading, in general, feels very slow;
- The game keeps your mouse cursor on the screen;
- There are several endings, but they're not much different, as they are only a few seconds long;
- The Invisible Enemy mode is just dumb, according to the director Shinji Mikami, it is supposed to be a challenging way to force players into changing their strategy, but I've beaten it on Hard with the same strategy as I've used before. After getting all endings and all achievements, you just memorize every enemy positions anyway. It just makes you die more often as you cannot tell how close the enemy is from you.

The resident evil game that aged like milk.

After the third time retrying the game from a previous save-point, i just get frustrated every time.

The bad:

-There is no indication where you're supposed to go, no dialogue log, hints or anything. Finish the game in 1 go or don't;
-The camera switches more than in the infamous catwoman scene;
-Tank controls are infuriating, especially with the camera constantly switching, causing controls to change each time, making you run in circles;
-DOORS, DOORS, DOORS... holy ♥♥♥♥ those doors.. for a game that makes you micromanage your inventory and makes you go back and forth, having more game time looking at door cutscenes than actual gameplay, that's just poor game design, even for back in the day;
-Aiming feels random and just plain bad, you can't see where you're aiming and have to hope for the best;
-keyboard and mouse controls are absolute ♥♥♥♥♥. Get grabbed? randomly bash direction keys and mouse keys to have a random chance of breaking free;
-Equipment management is ass, going in inventory to switch weapons, the "defensive items" system isn't thought out well;

The good:

-The only positive i can say about this remaster is that it is a remaster of the game that paved the road for other resident evil games. 

That's all, it didn't age well, generally the game has immense positive ratings of people with between 1 and 3 hours of gameplay on them. The game has been cleared by 22% of people with jill, 14% with chris and 9% with both. Barely any players have cleared it on normal or higher.

Don't be fooled by positive reviews, they are mostly people who bought it because of nostalgia. The gameplay's bad, the camera's horrible, graphics are mediocre, even for a remaster.

This game proves that the reason the actual remakes started at 2 for a reason, there isn't a lot of substance to start with, 2 and up were actually good games that were worth the effort to recreate.

Don't buy this unless you're an older fan wanting to replay you childhood game, watch a review instead or read some lore.

Gostei:
  - Muito bonito em todos os aspectos (menos nas CGs, não entendi pq não remasterizaram esse aspecto);
  - Jogabilidade atualizada, sendo bem mais fácil de controlar o personagem. Porém, para quem quer ter a experiência parecida com o jogo original, você pode escolher os comandos antigos;
  - Inimigos variados, tendo vários formas de enfrentá-los;
  - Dois personagens diferentes com momentos )alguns) diferentes no jogo;
  - Por mais que você possa se defender dos inimigos, ainda consegue dar medo ou pelo menos te deixar tenso;

Não gostei:
  - História poderia ser melhor contada, existem poucos diálogos e o que tem é bem básico;

Classic survival horror in HD;  
Refined with a some better textures and full HD resolution..
9.5/10

This game is still as good as it was when it was first for PS1 (I never played the gamecube/wii version) with updated graphics from the GC remake. You can play with a new modern controls or the tank controls and choose what graphics, resolution and more things in the settings (althoug there is few options).

[b] List of positive/negative things that I've noted at my first playthrough [/b]

[list] [b] Positive [/b]
[*] The game still feels like it's first release, with some minor tweaks/changes (like I've said, I've never played the GC/WII copy);
[*] Lets you choose what kind of FPS and if you want to play with original resolution or by 16:9;
[*] The game have some replayability (if you want to do the archivements or find about another endings or unlock all costumes/extra weapons) so you can wait some time and you will feel that your money is worth paying full price;
[*] Like I've said you get archivements, a leadboard (evem though I think it's already hacked because i've saw some people finish the game less than 10 min, until I see an video of that, I will not belive on that), and full support to the Xbox 360 gamepad (I do own one and played with him, felt great).

[b] Neutral [/b]
[*] The Crimson Head, Fuel Canister and Lighter (for Jill only, as Chris starts with the Lighter) are a good new thing, it makes you think even more if you should take that items with you (if you shot and kill the zombie) to evade the possibility of they reviving as Crimson Head's zombies, or you just don't have the space so you shouldn't kill and just evade zombies (but still it takes up to two inventory slots and if one inventory slot filled makes you even consider what should you take or not with you, think about two as Jill with lower Heath and Damage). I do think that this actually is a positive thing (but still I do not like them hehe) but it was not released when the first Resident Evil came out so some people may dislike and even rage more as the game is not hard enough as it is.

[b] Negative [/b]
[*] There are some issues in some areas of the game (mainly FPS drops). I did get rarely for the first part of the game, but in some parts or areas, my fps drops would go down for 25 FPS per second. It's probably not well optimised for some parts of the game or it's my CPU problem (but I don't belive in the latter as my CPU can handle more demaning games just fine, even being an Pentium G-3258 3,2 GHz [I didn't overclocked yet but this CPU is a Beast at 4-4,5 GHz, but still it can't compare to an i7] it should run well) I hope that they will bring some updates as it seems that some people are getting the same problem with better CPU's than mine. Also people complain about their mobile GPU's not working well, CAPCOM warned about that not being supported on the Requirements List of the game page but still they should look for some fix or update as many people also game on laptops (this last sentence is an opinion as not all laptop users had that problem but some complained about that in the forums);
[*] The lack of an type of Mercenarys or like Sega Saturn's release: Battle Game minigame after your first playthrough. It would be even better as you could even take more hours to the game;
[*] Some desynchronization in the cutscenes. It was not all the time, but from some of them have that problem;
[*] Some areas are low rendered. The detail in the overall it's great, but some wall's/textures/cutscenes were poorly upgraded to 1080p.
[/list]


[noparse] 
My final rating at this game : 8,0/10.

Why? Because it mantains the core of the game, with only few tweaks/changes/additions for the better on my perspective, but they should had more carefull updating the game to the modern day as they have some desynchronization and low rendered textures in some parts of the game. [/noparse]

The original [i]Resident Evil[/i] was released for PlayStation back in 1996 and it was a sucess, in 2002 Capcom remade the game for Nintendo Gamecube, they had improved the graphics, gameplay and added new stuff, items and puzzles, the new game, known as [b]Resident Evil REmake[/b] then took the original's game place in the story's timeline.
This one is the HD Remaster of the 2002 Gamecube remake, I'll point out a few pros and cons of this edition:

[b]Pros:[/b]

• Improved graphics, textures, creatures and character models;
• New grapphics settings that were not possible by the time of the original release;
• Support for 16:9 screens up to 4k (an edit on the game .ini file is required for resolutions bigger than 1080p);
• Support for 4:3 screens.
• Support for fixed 30, fixed 60 and variable framerates, good for all sorts of computers;
• Full Xbox 360 controller support, keyboard and mouse and as well two controll modes, one being the [i]classic[/i], that is similar to the Gamecube edition and the [i]alternate[/i], which is similar to the modern titles from the Resident Evil series;
• Good reply value, you can play several times to earn the different in-game unlockables (such as costumes and weapons) as well earn achievements.
• Several game modes to make the game harder and more interesting once you finish it once, you can also make it even easier should you prefer.

[b]Cons:[/b]

• Huge size, almost 20gb for a game that was originally played on two 1.5gb mini-discs;
• Doesn't have have native support for resolutions that are not 4:3 or 16:9, also some of the 16:9 resolutions are not avaliable at the game options and require to be manually changed at the .ini file;
• Background graphics have not received the same treatment as the characters and creatures, they look a bit blurry on higher resolutions, they're better than the Gamecube version though;
• Cutscenes were not remade at all, they look super blurry because they were stretched from 460p used by Gamecube;
• Not the best game to be played with keyboard and mouse, while it's still playable, a controller is highly recommended.


[b]My conclusion:[/b] 
The game is great, it has a great story, it can be hard for those who prefer and easy for those who don't.
You can play this for many hours to unlock everything and all achievements, so lots of fun for quite some time.
Minor graphics problems that won't ruin the game at all.
It's worth the 20 bucks, the game is great and brings back memories, also buying it will be enough to tell Capcom that we have interest in seeying the other RE games to be remade and brought to PC too.

[b]Note:[/b] [u]some people were not able to play the game due to slowdowns, even people with PCs far better than my own, some complained about audio issues or crashes, I got the game on pre-sale and played for about 9 hours and finished the game with Jill without a single audio, graphic and crash issue, therefore the game is working a 100% for me.[/u]

[b]Update:[/b] [i]fixed a few typing mistakes, english is not my main language and made a few mistakes that needed to be fixed.[/i]

14 years have passed since I played Resident Evil for the first time on my Playstation, and it still feels scary, lonely and freaking awesome. Even more at 1080p, 60fps and with a whole new physics made exclusively for Jill's boobs! Jiggle jiggle!

Pros; 
Great atmosphere;
Nostalgia all over the place; 
60fps and 1080p; 
It is hard as it should be, without that Hollywood-ish action nonsense. 

Cons; 
Textures can feel a little blurry from time to time; 
Voice acting still kind of sucks. 

